WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.199
- I have to read this from
here, because it's one

00:00:02.199 --> 00:00:03.874
of my favorite things
that you said in the book,

00:00:03.874 --> 00:00:06.940
obviously 'cause I'm in the
midst of a divorce right now,

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:08.082
which it's tough.

00:00:08.082 --> 00:00:12.018
And you wrote about having
to release what you thought

00:00:12.018 --> 00:00:14.591
of family was after getting divorced.

00:00:14.591 --> 00:00:16.434
And I'm going through that now.

00:00:16.434 --> 00:00:19.098
So I mean, I guess two questions it's like

00:00:19.098 --> 00:00:20.863
what is it about especially young girls

00:00:20.863 --> 00:00:23.058
'cause I remember reading
the fairytale thing,

00:00:23.058 --> 00:00:24.855
you know, we all think it's
going to happen one way.

00:00:24.855 --> 00:00:25.688
- Yeah.

00:00:25.688 --> 00:00:27.394
- And then reality sets in and it's hard.

00:00:27.394 --> 00:00:30.132
Like working at a marriage is very hard.

00:00:30.132 --> 00:00:31.813
And when you do experience divorce

00:00:31.813 --> 00:00:34.758
'cause I know you have an,
I am currently, I can't

00:00:34.758 --> 00:00:36.146
I think 'cause I'm in the middle of it.

00:00:36.146 --> 00:00:38.556
I can't even imagine doing it again.

00:00:38.556 --> 00:00:40.602
I can't imagine being married again.

00:00:40.602 --> 00:00:42.401
And one of my favorite things

00:00:42.401 --> 00:00:46.650
in your book was it took
five times for him to

00:00:46.650 --> 00:00:48.043
and I don't mean that in a funny way.

00:00:48.043 --> 00:00:49.153
I read that.

00:00:49.153 --> 00:00:51.775
Not as in like you were
making him kind of chase you.

00:00:51.775 --> 00:00:55.118
I read that as in like,
look, she knew, she knew

00:00:55.118 --> 00:00:57.491
that it was a big decision,
especially a blended family.

00:00:57.491 --> 00:00:59.212
I walked into that as
well with my marriage

00:00:59.212 --> 00:01:02.848
and it's a hard thing to
do when you walk into that.

00:01:02.848 --> 00:01:06.772
And I don't know, I love
that by the time you said yes

00:01:06.772 --> 00:01:08.129
he knew you meant it.

00:01:08.129 --> 00:01:08.962
- Right.

00:01:08.962 --> 00:01:09.795
- Yeah.

00:01:09.795 --> 00:01:11.896
And I mean, how did you rework this

00:01:11.896 --> 00:01:14.143
because I know a lot of women
out there that are in men

00:01:14.143 --> 00:01:17.925
that are divorced and maybe cannot imagine

00:01:17.925 --> 00:01:19.475
setting themselves up
for that again, you know?

00:01:19.475 --> 00:01:20.987
- You know, it took me a long time.

00:01:20.987 --> 00:01:24.423
It took me at least a year
to get on my feet again.

00:01:24.423 --> 00:01:25.978
I think it was, I had

00:01:25.978 --> 00:01:29.230
I didn't know anybody
that had been divorced.

00:01:29.230 --> 00:01:31.342
I felt like it was a failure on my part.

00:01:31.342 --> 00:01:32.240
I kept thinking.

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:33.073
- Yeah.

00:01:33.073 --> 00:01:34.610
- You know, I lost my self esteem

00:01:34.610 --> 00:01:36.575
because I kept thinking
what's wrong with me.

00:01:36.575 --> 00:01:39.447
Why couldn't I make this work, and.

00:01:39.447 --> 00:01:41.003
- There's so much shame
and guilt involved.

00:01:41.003 --> 00:01:41.836
- Yeah, exactly.

00:01:41.836 --> 00:01:42.669
- Yeah.

00:01:42.669 --> 00:01:45.086
- And then just unexpectedly.

00:01:47.394 --> 00:01:52.394
You know, I met Joe and it
was I had met him once before

00:01:52.501 --> 00:01:55.037
but it was kind of a blind
date when he called me.

00:01:55.037 --> 00:01:59.280
And then, but, you know,
I want to tell you Kelly,

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:00.343
I mean this is what I would say

00:02:00.343 --> 00:02:02.145
to you if I were your mother.

00:02:02.145 --> 00:02:02.978
- Yeah.

00:02:02.978 --> 00:02:03.811
- You know, my mother always said to me,

00:02:03.811 --> 00:02:05.739
things are gonna look better tomorrow.

00:02:05.739 --> 00:02:08.564
And if you can take one day at a time,

00:02:08.564 --> 00:02:10.081
and things will get better.

00:02:10.081 --> 00:02:14.128
And, you know, I look back on
it now and I think, you know,

00:02:14.128 --> 00:02:16.946
if I hadn't gotten divorced,
I never would have met Joe.

00:02:16.946 --> 00:02:20.217
I wouldn't have the
beautiful family I have now.

00:02:20.217 --> 00:02:21.050
- Yeah.

00:02:21.050 --> 00:02:24.752
- So I really think things
happen for the best.

00:02:24.752 --> 00:02:27.531
And I think Kelly, over
time, I don't know how long

00:02:27.531 --> 00:02:31.584
it's been for you, but I
think over time you heal

00:02:31.584 --> 00:02:34.764
and you're gonna be surprised

00:02:34.764 --> 00:02:37.468
and I can't wait until
that day comes for you.

00:02:37.468 --> 00:02:40.286
And you're going to call me
up and you're going to say,

00:02:40.286 --> 00:02:41.796
"Hey Jill, you were right."

00:02:41.796 --> 00:02:43.907
- Yeah, I was just kidding.

00:02:43.907 --> 00:02:44.740
Yeah.

00:02:45.591 --> 00:02:46.933
Well, it's just an amazing thing.

00:02:46.933 --> 00:02:49.835
I love reading that though
'cause it was like most,

00:02:49.835 --> 00:02:52.575
I think most women feel
pressure to say yes.

00:02:52.575 --> 00:02:54.090
And then you feel like you're like

00:02:54.090 --> 00:02:55.803
you don't love them if
you say no, I don't know.

00:02:55.803 --> 00:02:57.610
I just found that an amazing
thing that you took your time

00:02:57.610 --> 00:02:59.249
and we're like, let's make sure

00:02:59.249 --> 00:03:00.923
especially 'cause kids were involved.

00:03:00.923 --> 00:03:01.756
- Yeah.

00:03:01.756 --> 00:03:02.809
- And especially from the
situation that they were involved.

00:03:02.809 --> 00:03:04.893
- I love those boys so much.

00:03:04.893 --> 00:03:05.726
- Yeah.

00:03:05.726 --> 00:03:06.979
- And I tell Joe, that was
the reason I married him

00:03:06.979 --> 00:03:09.018
because I fell in love with the boys.

00:03:09.018 --> 00:03:11.683
- Yeah, that's so awesome.

00:03:11.683 --> 00:03:13.807
But I want to talk about
this too, because I know

00:03:13.807 --> 00:03:16.262
that you said cancer research
is really important to you.

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:17.737
We talked about that a minute ago,

00:03:17.737 --> 00:03:20.031
but and you've talked
about it quite a bit.

00:03:20.031 --> 00:03:21.623
And it's obviously a very
personal thing for you.

00:03:21.623 --> 00:03:23.510
It's a personal thing for all of us.

00:03:23.510 --> 00:03:24.777
Like you said, all

00:03:24.777 --> 00:03:27.516
of us are touched by
cancer, unfortunately.

00:03:27.516 --> 00:03:29.932
But I found it interesting
that you were very honest

00:03:29.932 --> 00:03:32.827
about losing faith
because I've lost people.

00:03:32.827 --> 00:03:33.849
And I know other people lost people

00:03:33.849 --> 00:03:37.242
and especially if I go into
like a children's hospital or

00:03:37.242 --> 00:03:39.458
and you see these young
little kids and you're like

00:03:39.458 --> 00:03:41.086
I don't understand this.

00:03:41.086 --> 00:03:43.956
Like I can't wrap my head
around why this is happening.

00:03:43.956 --> 00:03:46.899
And it's hard for people
to not lose faith.

00:03:46.899 --> 00:03:47.732
- Yes.

00:03:47.732 --> 00:03:48.948
- Like, you know, people generally do.

00:03:48.948 --> 00:03:51.402
So how do you still have
a very strong faith?

00:03:51.402 --> 00:03:53.860
Have you worked, you know,
through that or do you,

00:03:53.860 --> 00:03:55.704
did you have friends at home to do that?

00:03:55.704 --> 00:03:57.826
- Well, I don't know
whether your audience knows

00:03:57.826 --> 00:04:02.409
but we lost our son Beau to
cancer he was 46 years old.

00:04:03.852 --> 00:04:07.572
And I prayed so hard every single day

00:04:07.572 --> 00:04:09.077
that he was going to live.

00:04:09.077 --> 00:04:12.788
And I felt like he was such
a special person that he

00:04:12.788 --> 00:04:15.449
God would let him live and I just prayed

00:04:15.449 --> 00:04:18.755
and prayed and then it
just wasn't meant to be in.

00:04:18.755 --> 00:04:22.232
And when we lost Beau, it was hard

00:04:22.232 --> 00:04:26.404
for me to keep my faith because
I had believed so strongly

00:04:26.404 --> 00:04:29.680
in prayer and that he was,
you know, he'd make it.

00:04:29.680 --> 00:04:32.420
And it took me a long time Kelly

00:04:32.420 --> 00:04:36.836
and we were in a church
just like a year ago

00:04:36.836 --> 00:04:41.419
and he's, Beau's been gone,
gosh, almost six years.

00:04:41.419 --> 00:04:45.999
And a woman came up to me
in the church and she said,

00:04:45.999 --> 00:04:49.286
"Jill I want to be your prayer partner."

00:04:49.286 --> 00:04:50.677
And I said, prayer partner.

00:04:50.677 --> 00:04:53.005
I had never even heard
of a prayer partner.

00:04:53.005 --> 00:04:54.397
- I'm from the South I have.

00:04:54.397 --> 00:04:55.230
- So yeah.

00:04:55.230 --> 00:04:56.063
- Yeah.

00:04:56.063 --> 00:05:00.646
- And it was in the South
and so she started to call me

00:05:01.517 --> 00:05:03.276
and we would pray together.

00:05:03.276 --> 00:05:06.754
And to this day, I mean she
calls me maybe twice a week

00:05:06.754 --> 00:05:09.171
we email, we text one another

00:05:10.606 --> 00:05:13.223
and it really helped
me find my faith again.

00:05:13.223 --> 00:05:15.843
It was like, God was saying to me,

00:05:15.843 --> 00:05:19.093
"Okay, Jill you've had time come back."

00:05:20.101 --> 00:05:24.639
And so I felt that that was
a gift that she gave to me.

00:05:24.639 --> 00:05:27.345
- Yeah, and what a beautiful
way to actually be able

00:05:27.345 --> 00:05:28.282
to find your way back.

00:05:28.282 --> 00:05:30.606
I know a lot of people
still struggle with that.

